  "findings": [
    "command_schedule_canonical quantifies every ABCommands.Kind for each original Layout/Types; preserves the ordered unknown literal list and number of true fixed literals, not merely cardinality of unknowns.",
    "Known source soundness comes from the actual original Geometry and primary physical coloring. The canonical Types value is used only for folded schedule comparison; no host recoloring, no claim U and T graphs are equal.",
    "K16 internal rows are kernel-checked to contribute exactly five per foreign color. K15 retains its actual template type and the deleted vertex15 color; SameSchedule explicitly requires equality of every K15 type.",
    "All command constructors are covered, including concatenated freePair rows, full/tail domains, owner-dependent caps, high-proxy gates, and highTotal. Limits, gate atoms and polarity are type-independent because command itself depends only on Layout and Kind.",
    "For A, both foreign cells are K16 and marked K16, giving two free-size schedules. For B the left K15 bit remains, giving four schedules. This justifies six A/B schedules without conflating D."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This gate does not itself establish original Python fixed-source list equality, command execution order/allocator identity, complete finite folded schedule tables, or final native formula byte identity. Those subsequent bindings remain required.",
    "No independent compiler or finite computation rerun performed; accepted receipts and immutable source hashes checked."
  ],
